{"number": 1, "name": "S1.1 -- Every dispersion axis is data: tabulated and transcendental cases", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor 001 sec B 'Physics is pure data' at the axis level (.spec-md sec 3.1). Soft budget: 10-18 steps.\n\nWhat changes:\n- Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs: EpsAxisDispersion carries [<CustomEquality>] only because of EpsAxisEvaluated of (WaveLength -> ComplexRefractionIndex). It gains two kinds of data case:\n  (a) a TABULATED case: sorted wavelengths in metres, n and k arrays (a record marked [<NumericCarrier(...)>]), and an interpolation-rule union. The union has one case today: linear in lambda, clamped to the end samples, exactly what OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs buildTabulatedClosure computes.\n  (b) data cases for the four transcendental oscillator models (Tauc-Lorentz, Gaussian oscillator, Forouhi-Bloomer, Brendel-Bormann): their coefficients plus the abscissa scaling the finite-term cases already carry (DispersionFormula.wavelengthScale, and the reciprocal / eV convention of DispersionModels.fs AbscissaKind). They are evaluated in the core by the kernels that MOVE there from OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs (the four cases of DispersionModel.evaluate). The Domain's evaluate calls the moved kernel, so ONE implementation exists.\n- EpsAxisEvaluated and the custom Equals / GetHashCode are deleted, and structural equality returns.\n- DispersionModels.fs DispersionModel.toEpsAxis lowers the four models to the new data case (today it lowers to 'EpsAxisEvaluated this.evaluate'). Thermo-optic handling (ThermoOptic, evaluateAt) is unchanged: lowering stays isothermal.\n- Every match on the deleted case follows the new cases: LibraryFacets.fs (the 'Evaluated (transcendental)' facet key) and MaterialComplexityEditor.fs.\n- MaterialImport.fs entryFromTabulated produces EpsWithDispValue (IsotropicDispersive [one segment over the table's own range carrying the tabulated case]) with a complexity, and buildTabulatedClosure is deleted. Formula imports are untouched. (Making complexity mandatory is S1.2.)\n\nNo number moves.\n- BerremanTests EpsWithDispValueTests gains facts for the tabulated case (inside, both clamps, a single-sample table) and for each transcendental case, equal to the former closure at several wavelengths.\n- OpticalConstructor.Tests MaterialImportTests proves a tabulated refractiveindex.info page and an n,k CSV now carry data whose eps equals the old closure's, at and between the samples.\n- DispersionModelsTests stays green unchanged.\n\nGates: build and elevation; unit-tests by class (EpsWithDispValueTests, DispersionFormulaTests; Berreman/Berreman/** is in its applies_to); constructor-unit-tests; ui-tests for any Ui class whose fixture used the evaluated case.", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialImportTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs"], "invariants": ["ASSERT_INVARIANT s01-elev-list-empty must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"ELEV0\" -- Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s01-no-vstest must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk|xunit.runner.visualstudio|Xunit.SkippableFact|IsTestingPlatformApplication\" -- \"*.fsproj\" \"*.props\" \"*.targets\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s01-no-kit-kit-json must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"kit.kit-json\" -- Berreman/"]}
{"number": 2, "name": "S1.2 -- A material's physics is its complexity", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor .spec-md sec 3.2. Soft budget: 8-15 steps.\n\nAfter S1.1 every material is data, so:\n- MaterialLibrary.fs MaterialEntry: 'complexity : MaterialComplexity option' becomes 'complexity : MaterialComplexity'. The field 'properties : OpticalPropertiesWithDisp' is deleted and becomes a member 'properties' = complexity.toProperties, so readers keep compiling.\n- Every construction drops 'properties = ...' and 'Some'. The constructions are: the seeds in MaterialLibrary.fs (still present until S1.7), MaterialImport.fs, Report.fs (its 'complexity = None' record), the MaterialEditorView / MaterialEditorWindow / MaterialsWindowView save paths, and every fixture. 'git grep -n -E \"complexity = (None|Some)\" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor' lists them, among them DispersionModelsTests, LibraryFacetsTests, MaterialComplexityTests, MaterialProxyTests, OutOfBandDiagnosticTests, FsxAcceptanceTests, MaterialEditorWindowTests, MaterialsControlsTests, MaterialsWindowTests, NkDispersionChartTests and OutOfBandBadgeTests.\n- Every branch treating complexity = None as a coded, view-only preset is deleted, with nothing replacing it: the MaterialsControls.fs Edit-verb removal, the MaterialStore.fs coded-preset notes, and any None arm in OutOfBandDiagnostic, MaterialComplexityEditor and NkDispersionChart. Built-in protection arrives through provenance in S1.4 / S2.\n- MaterialStore.fs payloadOf compares the complexity directly. MaterialComplexityTests' 'no entry is left with complexity = None' fact becomes vacuous: delete it, naming its successor in the step's actions if one exists.\n\nNumbers are unchanged.\n\nGates: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests, ui-smoke, and ui-tests by touched class.", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/Report.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/MaterialsControls.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OutOfBandDiagnostic.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs"], "invariants": ["ASSERT_INVARIANT s02-elev-list-empty must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"ELEV0\" -- Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s02-no-vstest must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk|xunit.runner.visualstudio|Xunit.SkippableFact|IsTestingPlatformApplication\" -- \"*.fsproj\" \"*.props\" \"*.targets\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s02-no-kit-kit-json must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"kit.kit-json\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s02-no-eps-axis-evaluated must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"EpsAxisEvaluated\" -- Berreman/"]}
{"number": 3, "name": "S1.3 -- Every library entry is identified by a frozen GUID", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor .spec-md sec 3.3. Soft budget: 10-18 steps.\n\nPresets:\n- SourcePreset.id, DetectorPreset.id and PolarizerPreset.id (ElementId.fs, module Library) are ElementValueId strings today: \"src-600\", \"det-intensity\", \"pol-lp\" and the rest in SeedSources and seedEntries.\n- Each seeded preset gets a GUID minted ONCE as a fixed literal. Its ElementValueId becomes that GUID's string form, the convention LibraryEntry.entryId already uses for samples (s.id.toElementValueId). The grouping-tree leaves in seedTrees follow.\n- newSourceId (ElementId.fs) mints a plain GUID string, without the \"src-\" prefix.\n- Lookups by id (LibraryProxy.tryGetEntry, liveLibrary's Guid.TryParse sample branch) work for every GUID-identified entry.\n\nWell-known ids (.spec-md sec 3.3):\n- The preset GUID literals go in ONE Domain module beside MaterialIds (e.g. PresetIds). The sample GUID literals move out of SeedSamples into a SampleIds module beside them. MaterialIds and CategoryIds stay.\n- TableAndElementRotationView.fs 'module SeedEntryIds' (the default-scene and palette prebinds) is deleted, and its uses read the Domain module. This is a move, so one place names each built-in identity. Module names stay unique (ELEV015).\n\nTests: every literal preset id switches to the well-known members. 'git grep -n -E \"(src|det|pol)-[a-z0-9]\" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor' lists them, among them LibraryWindowTests, LightSourceEditorTests, WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests, SourceLibraryTests, SolverHandoffWindowTests, ExperimentProxyTests, PolarizerBehaviorTests, ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests, MainSceneMsgTests, WireUi0040CompositionTests, FsxAcceptanceTests, ExperimentControlsTests, SceneRoundTripTests, ExperimentCollectionProxyTests, LibraryProxyTests, EnvironmentRoundTripTests, WireUiCompositionTests and ScrollExtentTests. A fact asserting the old string shape asserts the GUID shape instead.\n\nAfterwards every entry kind (material, sample, category, source, detector, polarizer) has a GUID, which S1.4's envelope id relies on. No seeded preset string id remains anywhere in Berreman/*.fs: src-600, src-hene-..., det-intensity, det-ellipsometer, pol-lp, pol-cp-left, pol-cp-right and the rest, including facet codes such as 'FacetTreeNode_entry:src-600'. Later sections carry this as an invariant. Test-local user-source ids (e.g. 'src-mine') are not seeded ids and may stay.\n\nGates: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests, ui-smoke, and ui-tests by touched class.", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/Schematic.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs"], "invariants": ["ASSERT_INVARIANT s03-elev-list-empty must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"ELEV0\" -- Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s03-no-vstest must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk|xunit.runner.visualstudio|Xunit.SkippableFact|IsTestingPlatformApplication\" -- \"*.fsproj\" \"*.props\" \"*.targets\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s03-no-kit-kit-json must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"kit.kit-json\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s03-no-eps-axis-evaluated must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"EpsAxisEvaluated\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s03-complexity-mandatory must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"complexity = (None|Some)\" -- Berreman/"]}
{"number": 4, "name": "S1.4 -- Library entry files: envelope, provenance, canonical JSON, content hash, schemas", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor 001 sec A (the name rule, the library extensions, the catalogue layout) and sec B ('Every entry file carries', 'JSON Schema per kind', 'No up-converters'), with .spec-md sec 5. Soft budget: 15-25 steps.\n\nDomain (a new file after the library types):\n- LibraryEntryKind (material, sample, source, polarizer, detector, category; S7.1 adds the item-model kind) with int wire tags (value, tryOfWire) and an extension render: .material-json, .sample-json, .source-json, .polarizer-json, .detector-json, .category-json.\n- EntrySchema (kind + schema version).\n- EntryProvenance: built-in (catalogue id) / user / imported-from-kit (kit id) / pulled-from-source (source, record, source version, licence, citation); EntryLicence; EntryCitation; ContentHash (SHA-256 hex).\n- LibraryEntryEnvelope { schema; id (Guid); version (VersionNumber); name; category / facets; description; payload; provenance; contentHash }, with a payload union over the material physics, Sample, SourcePreset, DetectorPreset, PolarizerPreset and MaterialCategory. The envelope's id, name, category and description are the entry's own; the payload holds the rest.\n- CatalogueManifest (.catalogue-json): name, CatalogueId, catalogue version, and one row per entry (kind, id, version, file name, contentHash), with a manifest hash.\n- A built-in's protection derives from its provenance.\n\nStorage, canonical JSON (a new file compiled before ProjectJson.fs):\n- It OWNS the serializer options. ProjectJson.options and its private converters MOVE there, and ProjectJson calls them; the .ocproj aggregate itself stays until S4.4.\n- Canonical form: sorted object keys and invariant-culture shortest round-trip numbers, so every double round-trips bit-exactly.\n- contentHash = SHA-256 over the canonical form of the envelope WITHOUT its contentHash field.\n- The written file is indented canonical JSON. S2's database payload and S4's kit snapshot are those same bytes.\n\nStorage, entry files (a new file):\n- Serialize and parse one envelope per kind.\n- Parsing validates against the kind's JSON Schema FIRST. SchemaValidation.fs is generalised from the one project schema to a schema per kind, loaded by file name from schema/, which remains Content in OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj.\n- Then it checks schema.version against the app's, failing with a new typed StorageError case UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr (kind, found, expected). Then it checks the hash (ContentHashMismatchErr).\n- Schemas: material, sample, source, polarizer, detector, category and catalogue.\n- File names: the entry's name made filesystem-safe (.spec-md sec 3.11) + the kind's extension. Per-kind name uniqueness within a catalogue is a pure check, which export uses.\n\nTests (OpticalConstructor.Tests):\n- one round-trip fact per kind, over every MaterialComplexity shape (S1.1's tabulated and transcendental cases included), a multilayer Sample, a tunable source and a constant-Mueller polarizer;\n- the canonical form is key-order independent, and the hash is stable across write and read;\n- a wrong schema version gives the typed error, a tampered payload the hash mismatch, and a schema-invalid file SchemaValidationErr;\n- every built-in serialises and round-trips equal (builtInEntries, seedEntries and standardCategories are still present).\n\nGates: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests.", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/ProjectJson.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/Errors.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Lifecycle.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ProjectJsonRoundtripTests.fs"], "invariants": ["ASSERT_INVARIANT s04-elev-list-empty must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"ELEV0\" -- Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s04-no-vstest must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk|xunit.runner.visualstudio|Xunit.SkippableFact|IsTestingPlatformApplication\" -- \"*.fsproj\" \"*.props\" \"*.targets\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s04-no-kit-kit-json must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"kit.kit-json\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s04-no-eps-axis-evaluated must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"EpsAxisEvaluated\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s04-complexity-mandatory must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"complexity = (None|Some)\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s04-no-seeded-string-preset-ids must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"(src-(600|hene-|ar-4|ar-5|hecd-|diode-|ruby-|tisa-|ndyag-|er-1550|co2-|hg-|krf-|arf-|f2-1|euv-|beuv-|xe-mono|supercontinuum)|det-(intensity|ellipsometer)|pol-(lp|cp-left|cp-right))\" -- \"Berreman/*.fs\""]}
{"number": 5, "name": "S1.5 -- The built-in catalogue generated once from the code seeds", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor 001 sec B 'Shipped catalogue' (the generation half) and sec A 'Catalogue folder layout', with .spec-md secs 3.5-3.6. Soft budget: 6-12 steps.\n\nThe throw-away export:\n- A script Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/export-builtin.fsx loads the built Release x64 Domain and Storage assemblies. Through S1.4's serializer it writes Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/:\n  - ONE .catalogue-json: name 'Built-in', a fixed catalogue GUID, version 1, a row and hash per entry;\n  - one file per entry: every MaterialLibrary.builtInEntries material, every standardCategories category, every Library.SeedSamples.allSeedSamples sample, every SeedSources.allSeedSources source, and the detectors and polarizers of Library.seedEntries.\n- Every entry is version 1 with built-in provenance, its GUID and values exactly the seeds'. Names follow sec A (e.g. 'Silicon.material-json'), with no category folders.\n- The step runs the script and commits the folder. The script is deleted in THIS section once the parity test below is green.\n\nThe rest:\n- OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj copies ../Catalogue/Builtin/** to Catalogue/Builtin/ in its output (CopyToOutputDirectory, the precedent of its schema/*.json items; no new comment in the project file). The App (<install>/Catalogue/Builtin/), the TestWindows heads and both constructor test suites therefore carry the same files.\n- CatalogueProxy: a record and an in-memory double in Domain, and a folder create in Storage.\n  - Read reads a catalogue folder into a parsed catalogue: the manifest plus every envelope, each validated and hash-checked. A file missing from the manifest, or a manifest row with no file, is a typed error.\n  - Write writes a catalogue folder atomically (*.tmp, then replace).\n- Parity test (a new OpticalConstructor.Tests class): reading Catalogue/Builtin from the test output gives entries structurally equal to the code seeds (materials by complexity + metadata, samples, presets, categories) with the same GUIDs, and the manifest hash is stable. S1.7 deletes this class together with the seeds.\n- Confirm with git check-ignore that the new paths are committable ('[Bb]in/' does not match 'Builtin/').\n\nGates: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests.", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs", ".gitignore"], "invariants": ["ASSERT_INVARIANT s05-elev-list-empty must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"ELEV0\" -- Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s05-no-vstest must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk|xunit.runner.visualstudio|Xunit.SkippableFact|IsTestingPlatformApplication\" -- \"*.fsproj\" \"*.props\" \"*.targets\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s05-no-kit-kit-json must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"kit.kit-json\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s05-no-eps-axis-evaluated must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"EpsAxisEvaluated\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s05-complexity-mandatory must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"complexity = (None|Some)\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s05-no-seeded-string-preset-ids must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"(src-(600|hene-|ar-4|ar-5|hecd-|diode-|ruby-|tisa-|ndyag-|er-1550|co2-|hg-|krf-|arf-|f2-1|euv-|beuv-|xe-mono|supercontinuum)|det-(intensity|ellipsometer)|pol-(lp|cp-left|cp-right))\" -- \"Berreman/*.fs\""]}
{"number": 6, "name": "S1.6 -- CatalogueImport replaces seeding; the app and the tests load the catalogue", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor 001 sec B ('SeedingProxy / seedAll become CatalogueImport', 'tests load the same files') and .spec-md sec 3.4. Soft budget: 10-18 steps.\n\nMove the seam:\n- MOVE OpticalConstructor.Seeding/Seeding.fs into Domain as CatalogueImport.fs, compiled after SampleStore.fs.\n  - SeedingProxy becomes CatalogueImportProxy, with the same fields (saveCategory, saveMaterial, saveSample, saveLibraryEntry). SeedRejectedErr becomes the import error's case.\n  - seedAll becomes an orchestrator over the PARSED catalogue (S1.5's CatalogueProxy output). It pushes category, then material, then sample, then preset; the first error short-circuits.\n  - createInMemory (the empty in-memory stores bundle) stays as the test double.\n- Delete the OpticalConstructor.Seeding project: its folder, its .fsproj, its Berreman.slnx entry and every ProjectReference to it.\n- Re-point the seam's tests: RENAME_TEST SeedingProxyTests -> CatalogueImportProxyTests and SeedingInMemoryTests -> CatalogueImportInMemoryTests, renaming their files and Compile entries too. From S1.7 on an invariant forbids any 'SeedingProxy', 'seedAll' or 'OpticalConstructor.Seeding' text under Berreman/.\n\nCompose from the files:\n- AppContext.create (OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs) builds EMPTY in-memory stores (the createInMemoryEmpty variants). Before any window opens it imports Catalogue/Builtin from AppContext.BaseDirectory through CatalogueProxy + CatalogueImport. A load failure is logged and the app starts with what it has; nothing throws.\n- TableAndElementRotationView.fs DefaultStores (the test-scene default the TestWindows heads use) composes the same way.\n\nTest fixture:\n- One fixture file, module BuiltinCatalogue, compiled into BOTH OpticalConstructor.Tests and OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests by file link (AGENTS.md: share by linking).\n- It loads Catalogue/Builtin from the test output once, and exposes the filled stores and lookups by the well-known ids (MaterialIds, CategoryIds, SampleIds, PresetIds).\n\nThe seed VALUES stay until S1.7; this section only ends the app's and the fixture's need for them.\n\nGates: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests, ui-smoke, and ui-tests by touched class (AppContextTests, WireUiCompositionTests, MainWorkbenchTests).", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Seeding/Seeding.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Seeding/OpticalConstructor.Seeding.fsproj", "Berreman/Berreman.slnx", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SeedingProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SeedingInMemoryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj"], "invariants": ["ASSERT_INVARIANT s06-elev-list-empty must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"ELEV0\" -- Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s06-no-vstest must-find-nothing: git