{"number": 7, "name": "S1.7 -- The code seed values are deleted", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor 001 sec B ('...then the Domain seed values are deleted') and sec R ('The code seed values and seedAll's Domain source'), with .spec-md sec 3.3. Soft budget: 12-25 steps, mostly mechanical test re-pointing.\n\nDelete from Domain:\n- MaterialLibrary.builtInEntries with its builder helpers, and standardCategories;\n- Library.SeedSamples (its values; the ids moved to SampleIds in S1.3), SeedSources, seedEntries and seedTrees;\n- the self-seeding Library.createInMemory, and the self-seeding MaterialProxy / SampleProxy / CategoryProxy .createInMemory variants. Keep the empty stores, renaming them only if the plain name becomes free (ELEV015 / 019);\n- any seed experiment list that reads seeds (Experiments.seedExperiments).\n\nFollow-ups:\n- MaterialLibrary.tryFindCategory, tryFindCategoryByName and CategoryId.categoryName read standardCategories today. They resolve through a category list handed in instead (the CategoryProxy's listCategories). Every caller passes the live store; 'git grep -n -E \"categoryName|tryFindCategory\" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor' lists them.\n- LibraryProxy.libraryTrees: the 'By kind' grouping is DERIVED by a pure function over the library's entries (kind, then category / facet, then leaf). liveLibrary and its one product consumer (the 'model.library.libraryTrees ()' match in TableAndElementRotationView.fs) keep their shapes.\n- Re-point every test that reads a seed value to the BuiltinCatalogue fixture, a few files per step, numbers unchanged. 'git grep -l -E \"SeedSamples|builtInEntries|seedEntries|standardCategories|SeedSources\" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor' lists them (about 38 files across the two constructor suites).\n- Delete S1.5's parity class (DELETE_TEST without a successor; the bridge is gone). Add a catalogue-integrity fact in its place: every built-in file validates, the hashes match the manifest, ids are unique, and the expected kinds are present.\n- Schematic.fs and the colour map in TableAndElementRotationView.fs keep reading MaterialIds (the well-known ids stay).\n\nThis establishes 001 sec T 'From section 1'.\n\nGates: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests, ui-smoke, and ui-tests by touched class.", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/SampleStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/Schematic.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs"], "invariants": ["ASSERT_INVARIANT s07-elev-list-empty must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"ELEV0\" -- Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s07-no-vstest must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk|xunit.runner.visualstudio|Xunit.SkippableFact|IsTestingPlatformApplication\" -- \"*.fsproj\" \"*.props\" \"*.targets\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s07-no-kit-kit-json must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"kit.kit-json\" -- Berrema