{"number": 8, "name": "S2.1 -- The library model in EF Core, created without migrations", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor 001 sec C ('What it holds', 'What it never holds', 'Hybrid shape', 'No migrations') and sec R ('The Test EF table and its initial migration'), with .spec-md secs 3.18 and 5. Soft budget: 10-18 steps.\n\nOpticalConstructor.Database (C#, net10.0, x64):\n- Delete Test.cs, TestDbContext.cs and Migrations/ (the initial migration and its snapshot).\n- Add LibraryDbContext and its entities:\n  - an entry-version table keyed by (entry GUID, version): kind (int tag), name, lifecycle (int), protection (int), pin state (int), provenance kind, catalogue id, the canonical payload text (byte-identical to the S1.4 entry file) and its content hash;\n  - a latest-version row per entry (the local 'latest');\n  - facet-key rows (entry, version, key, value);\n  - sample-version to material-version rows;\n  - the catalogue-import log (catalogue id, folder, manifest hash, imported-at, entry count);\n  - pulled-source records (source, record path, source version or snapshot date / commit, licence, citation, the minted entry version), which S13 uses;\n  - a schema-stamp row.\n- Slow data only: nothing kit-, measurement- or preference-related (001 sec C's rule).\n\nCreation:\n- EnsureCreated, then the stamp is written. On open, a stamp different from the model's is a typed LibrarySchemaMismatchErr (found, expected), never a migration. The remedy is the caller's (S2.4).\n\nStorage references the Database project and owns the F# side:\n- open or create a context from a connection string. SQLite :memory: is kept open for the context's lifetime; file databases use WAL mode and one writer;\n- map entity to and from LibraryEntryEnvelope through S1.4's canonical JSON;\n- catch every EF call at this seam ([<ElevationBoundary(nameof StorageBoundary, ...)>] on the declarations) and map it to a typed error.\n\nRemovals:\n- OpticalConstructor.App/AppConfig.fs: delete ConfigKey.databaseProvider and ConfigKey.mssqlConnectionString (.spec-md sec 3.18); keep ConfigKey.sqliteConnectionString.\n- Delete OpticalConstructor.Tests/TestDbMigrationTests.fs, its fixtures/database-appsettings.json, and the test project's direct Database reference if nothing needs it.\n\nNew LibraryDatabaseTests:\n- create on :memory: writes the stamp, and a mismatch gives the typed error;\n- an entity round trip of every kind is byte-identical to its entry file;\n- the facet and sample-to-material rows.\n\nGates: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests.", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Database/OpticalConstructor.Database.csproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Database/TestDbContext.cs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Database/Test.cs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Database/Migrations/", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/AppConfig.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/TestDbMigrationTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Directory.Build.targets"], "invariants": ["ASSERT_INVARIANT s08-elev-list-empty must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"ELEV0\" -- Elevation