{"number": 9, "name": "S2.2 -- Pinned replaces VersionsInUse; SQLite materials and categories", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor 001 sec C ('Versions are immutable', 'Pinned replaces VersionsInUse', 'The library proxies keep their shapes and gain a SQLite create', 'Contract tests'). Soft budget: 14-24 steps.\n\nLifecycle.fs:\n- Delete VersionsInUse (with empty and usageOf) and VersionUsage.\n- Add PinState: VersionPinned | VersionUnpinned. It is one-way; a pinned version never unpins.\n- decideVersioning takes the stored version's PinState where it took VersionUsage: pinned + physics changed mints the next version; everything else behaves as today.\n- Delete Experiments.boundVersions and versionsInUseSeam, and fix their callers (AppContext.fs, tests).\n\nStores (MaterialStore.fs, SampleStore.fs):\n- keep a pin per version;\n- gain pin verbs on their proxies (e.g. pinMaterialVersion : MaterialVersionId -> Result<...>, pinSampleVersion);\n- refuse removal while any version is pinned: MaterialVersionInUseErr / SampleVersionInUseErr become ...PinnedErr with the same diagnostic payload;\n- take no VersionsInUse argument any more.\n\nSQLite create for MaterialProxy and CategoryProxy, in Storage, as type extensions whose names are unique per receiver (ELEV019), over S2.1's context. Every field is implemented against the entry-version rows:\n- latest = the latest row; resolveVersion looks up (id, version) whatever the lifecycle;\n- save applies decideVersioning with the stored pin;\n- mark inactive / active / supersede act on the latest version;\n- remove is refused when the material is referenced (the samples-referencing lookup reads the sample-to-material rows) or pinned;\n- categories list / add / update / remove, with the built-in-not-removable rule (a category from a built-in catalogue is protected).\n\nContract suites:\n- MaterialProxyTests and CategoryProxyTests become abstract suites with two concrete xUnit classes: one over the in-memory store and one over SQLite :memory: (ADD_TEST for the SQLite ones).\n- Every existing fact runs against both stores. Numbers are unchanged, and the count rises.\n\nGates: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests, and ui-tests by touched class.", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Lifecycle.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/SampleStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CategoryProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LifecycleTests.fs"], "invariants": ["ASSERT_INVARIANT s09-elev-list-empty must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"ELEV0\" -- Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s09-no-vstest must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk|xunit.runner.visualstudio|Xunit.SkippableFact|IsTestingPlatformApplication\" -- \"*.fsproj\" \"*.props\" \"*.targets\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s09-no-kit-kit-json must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"kit.kit-json\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s09-no-eps-axis-evaluated must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"EpsAxisEvaluated\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s09-complexity-mandatory must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"complexity = (None|Some)\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s09-no-seeded-string-preset-ids must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"(src-(600|hene-|ar-4|ar-5|hecd-|diode-|ruby-|tisa-|ndyag-|er-1550|co2-|hg-|krf-|arf-|f2-1|euv-|beuv-|xe-mono|supercontinuum)|det-(intensity|ellipsometer)|pol-(lp|cp-left|cp-right))\" -- \"Berreman/*.fs\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s09-no-seeding-seam must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"SeedingProxy|seedAll|OpticalConstructor.Seeding\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s09-t1-no-code-seeds must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"let (builtInEntries|seedEntries|standardCategories) \" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s09-no-seed-modules must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"SeedSamples|SeedSources|SeedEntryIds\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s09-no-test-db must-find-nothing: git grep -n -w -E \"TestDbContext|DatabaseProvider|databaseProvider|OpticalConstructorMssql\" -- Berreman/"]}
{"number": 10, "name": "S2.3 -- SQLite samples, sources, presets and the live library", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nS2.2's rules, for the remaining library proxies. Soft budget: 12-20 steps.\n\nSQLite create for:\n- SampleProxy: versioned; saving writes the sample-to-material-version rows from the structure's MaterialVersionIds; pin; remove refused while pinned.\n- SourceProxy: user sources, versioned in the database though the proxy surface stays unversioned. Save mints per decideVersioning against the pin; tryGetSource returns the latest; protected presets are refused as today (ProtectedSourceRefusedErr).\n- The preset store, Library.LibraryEntryStore (proxy + addEntry), for detectors, polarizers and built-in sources.\n- The LibraryProxy live view, reading the database: Library.liveLibrary's composition (presets + live samples + user sources) with S1.7's derived trees.\n\nContract suites run against BOTH stores for SampleProxyTests, the proxy part of SourceLibraryTests, LibraryProxyTests, and the preset store (in LibraryProxyTests or a new class).\n\nThe in-memory stores stay the doubles. CatalogueImport (S1.6) writes into either.\n\nGates: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests, and ui-tests by touched class.", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstruc