{"number": 11, "name": "S2.4 -- Database location, settings, backup and restore; the app runs on the database", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor 001 sec C 'Settings' and sec G ('Library database', 'Every path is overridable'), with .spec-md sec 3.9 and the DataLocations shape in sec 5. Soft budget: 10-18 steps.\n\nDataLocations (Domain, WorkbenchSettings.fs) holds every location:\n- the library connection string, default 'Data Source=%LOCALAPPDATA%/Softellect/Berreman/OpticalConstructor/library.db', with environment variables expanded at read;\n- Backups/ beside the database;\n- the preferences folder %APPDATA%/Softellect/Berreman/OpticalConstructor/;\n- the suggested kits parent, Documents/Optical Constructor/Kits/;\n- exports, Documents/Optical Constructor/Exports/, which AppContext.create already builds for experimentExport and now reads from here;\n- the catalogue export folder, Documents/Optical Constructor/Catalogues/;\n- the shipped catalogue, <install>/Catalogue/.\nEach is an appsettings.json key read once by AppConfig.loadWorkbenchSettings through the WorkbenchSettingsDoors pattern; the connection string uses tryGetConnectionString on ConfigKey.sqliteConnectionString. Missing keys are written back as today.\n\nAppContext.create composes the SQLite library proxies over DataLocations' connection string:\n- A fresh database is created (EnsureCreated + stamp) and Catalogue/Builtin is imported through CatalogueImport.\n- LibrarySchemaMismatchErr is shown, never silently recreated. The Launcher offers 'Recreate library from catalogues': the old file is first copied into Backups/, then deleted and recreated.\n- Tests never reach the user's file: every test composition (AppContextTests, the WireUi*CompositionTests, MainWorkbenchTests, the FsxAcceptanceTests bench) passes :memory: or a file under the test output.\n\nBackup and restore (Storage):\n- 'Back up library now...' runs VACUUM INTO a timestamped file in Backups/.\n- 'Restore library...' picks a backup and asks for confirmation. It backs up the current database first, then replaces it and reopens (.spec-md sec 10).\n- Both are Library-window buttons (LibraryWindowView.fs) with ConstructorUiId ids and semantic messages. Their Storage functions are tested on a file database under the test output.\n\nGates: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests, ui-smoke, and ui-tests by touched class.", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/WorkbenchSettings.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/AppConfig.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/appsettings.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs"], "invariants": ["ASSERT_INVARIANT s11-elev-list-empty must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"ELEV0\" -- Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s11-no-vstest must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk|xunit.runner.visualstudio|Xunit.SkippableFact|IsTestingPlatformApplication\" -- \"*.fsproj\" \"*.props\" \"*.targets\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s11-no-kit-kit-json must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"kit.kit-json\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s11-no-eps-axis-evaluated must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"EpsAxisEvaluated\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s11-complexity-mandatory must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"complexity = (None|Some)\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s11-no-seeded-string-preset-ids must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"(src-(600|hene-|ar-4|ar-5|hecd-|diode-|ruby-|tisa-|ndyag-|er-1550|co2-|hg-|krf-|arf-|f2-1|euv-|beuv-|xe-mono|supercontinuum)|det-(intensity|ellipsometer)|pol-(lp|cp-left|cp-right))\" -- \"Berreman/*.fs\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s11-no-seeding-seam must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"SeedingProxy|seedAll|OpticalConstructor.Seeding\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s11-t1-no-code-seeds must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"let (builtInEntries|seedEntries|standardCategories) \" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s11-no-seed-modules must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"SeedSamples|SeedSources|SeedEntryIds\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s11-no-test-db must-find-nothing: git grep -n -w -E \"TestDbContext|DatabaseProvider|databaseProvider|OpticalConstructorMssql\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s11-no-versions-in-use must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"VersionsInUse|versionsInUseSeam\" -- Berreman/"]}
{"number": 12, "name": "S3.1 -- Import on every start and the per-entry decision table", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor 001 sec B ('Import on every start', the per-entry decision table, and the read side of 'Extra catalogue folders'), with .spec-md secs 3.7-3.8. Soft budget: 12-22 steps.\n\nDomain CatalogueImport gains a pure decision function over (the incoming envelope; what the library holds for its id and for its name). It returns one ImportDecision per entry, exactly 001 sec B's rows:\n- new id: add;\n- same id, same hash: reuse;\n- same id, a version not held locally: add that version. The local latest moves only for a protected built-in from a catalogue;\n- same id and version, a different hash: a divergence, imported as a flagged fork under a new id (provenance keeps the original id);\n- different id, same name: side by side ('Si -- from A'), with an explicit re-binding choice;\n- an entry the catalogue no longer lists: InactiveEntry, still resolvable.\nEach row carries its default action and the alternatives the dialog offers. The apply function takes the confirmed rows and writes through the stores; nothing else writes.\n\nStart-up import:\n- For the shipped catalogue and every folder in the import log, compare the manifest hash with the logged one, and skip when they are equal.\n- Otherwise decide every entry and apply the rows that overwrite nothing (add, reuse, add version, mark inactive), then log the import.\n- Rows needing a choice (divergence, name collision) are held in the AppContext as pending decisions for S3.2's dialog.\n- 'Register catalogue folder...' (Library window) imports a read-only folder and logs it. Unregistering removes the log row; its entries stay, because user data never vanishes silently.\n\nTests: one fact per decision row over the in-memory stores and the same rows over SQLite :memory:; the manifest-hash skip; a changed built-in catalogue mints the new version and moves the latest; a user entry is never touched (001 Summary).\n\nGates: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests, and ui-tests by touched class.", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Lifecycle.fs"], "invariants": ["ASSERT_INVARIANT s12-elev-list-empty must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"ELEV0\" -- Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s12-no-vstest must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk|xunit.runner.visualstudio|Xunit.SkippableFact|IsTestingPlatformApplication\" -- \"*.fsproj\" \"*.props\" \"*.targets\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s12-no-kit-kit-json must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"kit.kit-json\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s12-no-eps-axis-evaluated must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"EpsAxisEvaluated\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s12-complexity-mandatory must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"complexity = (None|Some)\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s12-no-seeded-string-preset-ids must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"(src-(600|hene-|ar-4|ar-5|hecd-|diode-|ruby-|tisa-|ndyag-|er-1550|co2-|hg-|krf-|arf-|f2-1|euv-|beuv-|xe-mono|supercontinuum)|det-(intensity|ellipsometer)|pol-(lp|cp-left|cp-right))\" -- \"Berreman/*.fs\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s12-no-seeding-seam must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"SeedingProxy|seedAll|OpticalConstructor.Seeding\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s12-t1-no-code-seeds must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"let (builtInEntries|seedEntries|standardCategories) \" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s12-no-seed-modules must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"SeedSamples|SeedSources|SeedEntryIds\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s12-no-test-db must-find-nothing: git grep -n -w -E \"TestDbContext|DatabaseProvider|databaseProvider|OpticalConstructorMssql\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s12-no-versions-in-use must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"VersionsInUse|versionsInUseSeam\" -- Berreman/"]}
{"number": 13, "name": "S3.2 -- The import dialog and single-file drop", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor 001 sec B ('The decisions show as one dialog with a row per entry'), sec H ('A library entry: its -json file, dropped onto the Library or Materials window') and sec O 'Import dialog'. Soft budget: 10-18 steps.\n\nThe dialog (a new window with its own view and window files in OpticalConstructor.Ui):\n- One row per entry: name, kind, version, status (the decision), the default action, and an override picker (fork / side by side / re-bind 'use my X instead', with a diff preview of the two payloads).\n- Apply and Cancel share a row (.spec-md sec 10.5). It is pure MVU over the decision rows: Apply dispatches the apply message, and nothing changes before it.\n- It calls WindowFit.keepOnScreen, joins ScrollExtentTests, and has ConstructorUiId ids (e.g. ImportDecisionList, ImportApplyButton).\n\nOpeners:\n- S3.1's pending decisions open it from the Launcher.\n- Dropping one or more entry files of any kind onto the Library or Materials window parses them (S1.4) and opens it.\n- S4.2 reuses it for kit snapshots.\n\nThe decide / override / apply / cancel messages are semantic. ui-tests drive them headless, and ui-smoke renders the view.\n\nGates: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests, ui-smoke, and ui-tests by touched class.", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/WindowLayout.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs"], "invariants": ["ASSERT_INVARIANT s13-elev-list-empty must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"ELEV0\" -- Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s13-no-vstest must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk|xunit.runner.visualstudio|Xunit.SkippableFact|IsTestingPlatformApplication\" -- \"*.fsproj\" \"*.props\" \"*.targets\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s13-no-kit-kit-json must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"kit.kit-json\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s13-no-eps-axis-evaluated must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"EpsAxisEvaluated\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s13-complexity-mandatory must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"complexity = (None|Some)\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s13-no-seeded-string-preset-ids must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"(src-(600|hene-|ar-4|ar-5|hecd-|diode-|ruby-|tisa-|ndyag-|er-1550|co2-|hg-|krf-|arf-|f2-1|euv-|beuv-|xe-mono|supercontinuum)|det-(intensity|ellipsometer)|pol-(lp|cp-left|cp-right))\" -- \"Berreman/*.fs\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s13-no-seeding-seam must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"SeedingProxy|seedAll|OpticalConstructor.Seeding\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s13-t1-no-code-seeds must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"let (builtInEntries|seedEntries|standardCategories) \" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s13-no-seed-modules must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"SeedSamples|SeedSources|SeedEntryIds\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s13-no-test-db must-find-nothing: git grep -n -w -E \"TestDbContext|DatabaseProvider|databaseProvider|OpticalCo