{"number": 15, "name": "S4.1 -- The kit file, KitFolder, KitProxy and KitContext", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor 001 sec E (a kit is a folder; the kit file; atomic writes; concurrency: the lock and external changes), sec A (the kit layout and the name rule), and sec P (KitProxy, KitContext, ClockProvider), with .spec-md secs 3.11-3.12 and 5. Soft budget: 14-24 steps.\n\nDomain Kit.fs (module Kit):\n- KitId (GUID), KitName, KitAuthor, KitNotes.\n- KitFile, the .kit-json: id, name, author, created, modified, notes, and the sendExclude globs. S8.3 adds the naming template and S9.2 the import profiles.\n- KitFolder (the folder path type); KitRelativePath (forward slashes, never absolute, never escaping the kit); KitAccess (read-write / read-only); ClockProvider (an injected now); the filesystem-safe name rule as a member.\n\nDomain KitProxy record (Result-returning functions):\n- read and write the kit file;\n- list, read, write and delete kit files per kind, generic over the kind's extension so later kinds add no verbs (experiment and setup files arrive in S4.3);\n- read a data file by relative path with its SHA-256; copy a file in (S4.2); write and list snapshots (S4.2);\n- acquire and release .oc/lock (machine, user, process id, time). A foreign live lock is KitLockedErr carrying the holder, and the caller can then open read-only;\n- the external-change check: the stamps recorded at load against the folder now, giving the changed kit files.\n\nImplementations:\n- KitProxy.createInMemory, in Domain.\n- KitProxy.create (folder : KitFolder), in a new Storage file: atomic writes (*.tmp, then replace); .oc/ created on first write; every IO exception mapped to a typed error.\n- A read-only KitContext writes nothing at all, not even .oc/ (.spec-md sec 3.12).\n\nKitContext (Domain) holds the proxy, the loaded KitFile, the access and the clock.\n\nInitialising a folder (used by S4.3 and S5.2):\n- An empty folder gets .kit-json + data/ + library/. A non-empty folder keeps every file and gets the same additions (001 sec F 'New kit...').\n- kit.schema.json is validated on read; a version mismatch is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr.\n\nTests: ONE contract suite run over the in-memory proxy and over a folder under the test output. It covers lock contention between two proxies on one folder, a read-only context writing nothing, atomic replace, change detection, and initialising empty and non-empty folders.\n\nGates: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests.", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/Errors.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Units.fs"], "invariants": ["ASSERT_INVARIANT s15-elev-list-empty must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"ELEV0\" -- Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s15-no-vstest must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk|xunit.runner.visualstudio|Xunit.SkippableFact|IsTestingPlatformApplication\" -- \"*.fsproj\" \"*.props\" \"*.targets\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s15-no-kit-kit-json must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"kit.kit-json\" -- B