{"number": 16, "name": "S4.2 -- Attachments by relative path and hash; the library snapshot and its resolution", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor 001 sec E ('References inside a kit are relative paths...', 'Attaching a file from outside...', 'Lab files are read-only', 'Library closure snapshot', 'Resolution on open') and sec A's library/<id>@v<n>.<kind>-json. Soft budget: 12-22 steps.\n\nAttachments:\n- DataAttachment (Domain Kit) is a KitRelativePath + the ContentHash recorded at attach.\n- A file inside the kit is recorded in place. A file outside is copied into data/ (or a chosen subfolder of it) keeping its name, with ' (2)', ' (3)'... on collision. The app never writes a lab file.\n- A status function compares the recorded hash with the file now: unchanged, data changed since attach, or missing. It runs on open and before each fit (S11).\n- Experiments.DataFilePath (an absolute path string today) is replaced by DataAttachment in Experiment.dataFileOpt and attachDataFile. ExperimentDataStore.createFileBacked and ExperimentDataLoad.loadAndValidate read through the kit by relative path. No kit file stores an absolute path.\n\nSnapshot:\n- When a kit first references a library version (binding a sample, material or preset; item models later), its entry file is written byte-identical to library/<id>@v<n>.<kind>-json, and the version is PINNED in the database (S2.2). Built-ins are included.\n\nResolution on open (pure Domain, REUSING S3.1's decision function over the snapshots against the database):\n- same id, version and hash: the database entry;\n- missing locally: the snapshot, read-only, with 'Add to my library';\n- divergence: reported, and the kit keeps its snapshot;\n- a name-only collision: side by side, with an explicit re-binding.\nThe rows go to S3.2's dialog, and nothing in the database changes unconfirmed. The session's library is the database view overlaid with the kit's read-only snapshot entries (a LibraryProxy composition), so the kit opens on any machine.\n\nTests: attach in place, copy-in, the collision suffix, changed, missing; a snapshot written once per version and pinned; every resolution row; a kit opened against an EMPTY library resolves every entry from library/.\n\nGates: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests.", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataProxy.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/ExperimentDataStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs"], "invariants": ["ASSERT_INVARIANT s16-elev-list-empty must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"ELEV0\" -- Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s16-no-vstest must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk|xunit.runner.visualstudio|Xunit.SkippableFact|IsTestingPlatformApplication\" -- \"*.fsproj\" \"*.props\" \"*.targets\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s16-no-kit-kit-json must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"kit.kit-json\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s16-no-eps-axis-evaluated must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"EpsAxisEvaluated\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIAN