{"number": 21, "name": "S5.3 -- The kit window: title, Kit menu, lock, reload and mode; Data locations", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor:\n- 001 sec O: the title shows the kit name and folder; the Kit menu with Show in Explorer, Reload changes and Close kit (S6 adds Send kit... and Copy experiments...);\n- sec E 'Concurrency': one window per kit, the lock warning with 'open read-only', and on activation the offer to reload files changed outside the app;\n- sec F: 'Inside a kit the mode can be switched';\n- sec G: 'a Launcher Data locations panel shows them, each with Open folder'.\nSoft budget: 10-18 steps.\n\n- One window per kit: opening a kit that is already open activates its window.\n- Lock: a foreign lock (S4.1 KitLockedErr) shows the holder's machine, user and time, with 'Open read-only' and Cancel on one row (.spec-md sec 10.5). Read-only shows in the title and disables every write message.\n- Reload: on window activation, run S4.1's external-change check. Changed files are listed with 'Reload' (re-read them into the model) and 'Keep mine'. 'Reload changes' in the Kit menu runs the same check on demand.\n- Mode switch: a forward / inverse toggle in the kit window that keeps the kit and the model. It uses the WindowMode.fs vocabulary if that fits, otherwise a two-case union.\n- Data locations: a window opened from a Launcher footer link. It lists every DataLocations entry with its path and 'Open folder', which opens Ex