{"number": 22, "name": "S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor 001 sec H (a kit; Send kit... / Open kit from zip...; between kits), sec E ('Large lab files... Send kit... honours sendExclude') and sec P (KitArchiveProxy, SendKit, OpenKitZip), with .spec-md sec 3.15. Soft budget: 12-22 steps.\n\nKitArchiveProxy (a record and an in-memory implementation in Domain; a Storage create over System.IO.Compression):\n- Zip a kit folder into one <kit name>.zip, excluding .oc/ and every sendExclude glob. The globs use a small pure matcher in Domain supporting **, * and ?; no new package is added (STL pins no globbing package).\n- Unzip into a chosen target folder, refusing any entry that escapes it.\n- Exceptions are mapped at the seam.\n\nThe UI:\n- 'Send kit...' in the Kit menu, through a save dialog defaulting to the DataLocations exports folder.\n- 'Open kit from zip...' on the start screen: choose a zip and a target folder, extract, then open as S5.2 does.\n- Messages SendKit and OpenKitZip; ids SendKitButton and OpenKitZipButton.\n\n'Copy experiments from another kit...' (Kit menu):\n- Pick a kit folder (the source opens read-only) and pick experiments.\n- Each experiment is copied with its setup files, the data files it references (into data/, under S4.2's collision rule, hashes re-recorded) and the library snapshots it needs. Clashing names get S4.1's suffix rule.\n- S7.2 adds the item mapping once items exist.\n\nTests: the zip honours .oc/ and the globs (e.g. '**/*.dng'); unzip + reopen equals the original kit file by file; a copy brings exactly the referenced files.\n\nGates: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests, ui-smoke, and ui-tests by touched class.", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs"], "invariants": ["ASSERT_INVARIANT s22-elev-list-empty must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"ELEV0\" -- Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s22-no-vstest must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk|xunit.runner.visualstudio|Xunit.SkippableFact|IsTestingPlatformApplication\" -- \"*.fsproj\" \"*.props\" \"*.targets\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s22-no-kit-kit-json must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"kit.kit-json\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s22-no-eps-axis-evaluated must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"EpsAxisEvaluated\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s22-complexity-mandatory must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"complexity = (None|Some)\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s22-no-seeded-string-preset-ids must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"(src-(600|hene-|ar-4|ar-5|hecd-|diode-|ruby-|tisa-|ndyag-|er-1550|co2-|hg-|krf-|arf-|f2-1|euv-|beuv-|xe-mono|supercontinuum)|det-(intensity|ellipsometer)|pol-(lp|cp-left|cp-right))\" -- \"Berreman/*.fs\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s22-no-seeding-seam must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"SeedingProxy|seedAll|OpticalConstructor.Seeding\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s22-t1-no-code-seeds must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"let (builtInEntries|seedEntries|standardCategories) \" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/", "ASSERT_INVARIAN