{"number": 23, "name": "S7.1 -- Items, parameters and item models", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor 001 sec I (items; ItemModel and its table; Parameter / ParameterState; dial mapping; revisions; material parameters as unknowns, whose study half is S11.1), with .spec-md secs 3.14, 3.17 and 3.23. Soft budget: 16-28 steps.\n\nDomain Kit, the Item:\n- ItemId (GUID) and ItemLabel ('LP1', 'CPL2', 'QZ', 'Phone').\n- The model it instantiates: a preset, a SampleVersionId, or an ItemModel version (.spec-md sec 3.14).\n- Its own Parameter values; an optional photo (a KitRelativePath to a kit file) and notes; a revision number with a short value history.\n- Parameter = a ParameterName (reuse MuellerInverse.ParameterName) + a ParameterState: KnownParameter value | UnknownParameter start * bounds * prior option | CalibratedParameter value * sigma * from-fit-run.\n- Dial mapping: a rotatable item has a zero (an ordinary parameter) and a sign (REUSE MuellerReconstruction.DialSign). Experiments record raw dial readings.\n\nNoise data (.spec-md sec 3.23): MOVE AngleUncertainty, ElementUncertainty, ThroughputUncertainty and NoiseParam (with decentLab and noiseless) from BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs into Domain. The harness opens them from there, and its numbers are unchanged.\n\nThe ItemModel library kind (LibraryEntryKind gains it; .item-model-json with a schema). Its payload is a union over 001 sec I's parameterised rows:\n- light source: over a source preset's lambda, the output polarization (azimuth, ellipticity, degree of polarization) and an intensity scale;\n- real linear polarizer: extinction ratio or diattenuation, and an axis offset;\n- retarder plate: retardance delta (dispersive where the model says so) and a fast-axis offset;\n- compound in light order: a list of component models with offsets, generalising ConstantMueller (e.g. CPL = LP . Retarder(45 deg + Delta, delta));\n- black-box Mueller: 16 parameters, or 15 + scale, at reference orientation, rotated as R(-phi) M R(phi);\n- empty slot: identity;\n- intensity detector: a session-scoped gain, a dark offset and a noise model;\n- Mueller polarimeter and ellipsometer: a noise model (NoiseParam).\nThe ideal LP / CP presets and the stack sample are the existing entries and get no wrapper.\n\nGenerated parameters: each model kind publishes its parameter axes (names, kinds, defaults), so the fitter's axis list is generated, never hand-written. An item's parameters are created from them.\n\nThe item-model store:\n- a proxy record, an in-memory implementation, and a SQLite create, with the contract suite run on both (the S2 pattern);\n- CatalogueImport gains saveItemModel;\n- the built-in item models (real LP, retarder, CPL compound, black-box Mueller, empty slot, intensity detector, polarimeter, ellipsometer) are written once through the export path and added to Catalogue/Builtin/ with the manifest updated. There is no code seed.\n\nKit files and updates:\n- <label>.item-json kit files go through KitProxy (schema + version). Referencing a model version snapshots and pins it (S4.2).\n- Pure updates for AddItem, SetParameterState, and publishing a revision (which S11.5 uses).\n\nGates: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests, and unit-tests by class for the BerremanTests classes that open the moved noise types. Name the cheapest classes that compile and exercise them.", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-fi