{"number": 25, "name": "S8.1 -- The run law walks every object; the source is real", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor 001 sec N ('The run law walks any number of objects', 'The source is real', 'One item-model evaluator') and sec R ('measuredElementOf and the first polarizer sets unit intensity special case'). Soft budget: 12-22 steps.\n\nExperimentRun.fs:\n- The fold walks the light path slot by slot, in light order, through each element's Mueller matrix. Any number of samples (objects) sit in series, and each decides its own capture branch (T / R) for the path the detector is on.\n- The 'first polarizer before the first sample sets a unit-intensity state' rule (detectorStokes's prepared flag) is deleted. The source emits its own Stokes state x intensity scale.\n- The source's DEFAULT parameter set (unpolarized, with the unit scale applied after the first polarizer as today) reproduces every existing chart exactly.\n\nThe host:\n- TableAndElementRotationView.fs measuredElementOf ('the first bound sample') is deleted.\n- The host hands ExperimentRun every object on the detector's BeamLayout path, each solved at its drawn incidence and spin (Propagation.sampleMuellerSpun).\n\nOne item-model evaluator (Domain): model x parameters x orientation x lambda gives a MuellerMatrix.\n- Stack samples go through Berreman: Propagation.sampleMuellerSpun on the table; MuellerInverse.orientForCut + createBerremanForward for cut plates.\n- Polarizer presets go through Propagation.behaviorMueller.\n- Black-box, compound, retarder and real-LP models go through the Stokes-Mueller algebra, REUSING MuellerReconstruction.retarderMueller and the existing rotation helpers.\n- A detector's gain and dark belong to S11.2's forward model, not here.\n\nProof:\n- ExperimentRunTests gains facts: two samples in series apply M2 . M1; the capture branch is decided per object; the default source equals the old unit-intensity rule on every existing case.\n- PolarizerBehaviorTests, PropagationTests and the FsxAcceptanceTests classes (under ui-tests) stay numerically unchanged.\n\nGates: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests, ui-smoke, and ui-tests (FsxAcceptanceTests, ExperimentControlsTests, MainWorkbenchTests and the touched classes). kit-acceptance does not exist yet.", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentRun.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Propagation.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/BeamLayout.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentRunTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PolarizerBehaviorTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs"], "invariants": ["ASSERT_INVARIANT s25-elev-list-empty must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"ELEV0\" -- Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s25-no-vstest must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk|xunit.runner.visualstudio|Xunit.SkippableFact|IsTestingPlatformApplication\" -- \"*.fsproj\" \"*.props\" \"*.targets\