{"number": 26, "name": "S8.2 -- Setups as slots", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor 001 sec J ('Setup = an ordered optical path of slots...', 'Experiments reference setups (name + revision). The ElementDescriptor list becomes the slot list.') and sec P (CreateSetup, AssignSlot, SwapSlot). Soft budget: 12-22 steps.\n\nDomain Setup { name : SetupName; revision; slots }:\n- Slot roles: Source, Prep 1..k, Object 1..n (two or more samples in series), Analyzer 1..k, Detector.\n- Each slot holds an item (ItemId) or nothing, plus its position on the beam and R1 / R2 / R3, or a dial reading.\n- <name>.setup-json (schema + version) REPLACES S4.3's scene file shape. Scene.SceneSnapshot, and whatever only it used, is deleted; the constructor's scene save / load becomes setup save / load.\n\nExperiments:\n- Experiment.setup : ElementDescriptor list becomes a setup reference (name + revision). ElementDescriptor, ElementBinding and PlacementSummary go wherever a slot carries the same facts.\n- Experiments keep their captured-snapshot meaning through the setup revision: editing a setup that an experiment uses mints the next revision.\n\nThe table:\n- It draws the ACTIVE setup: slots map to table elements, with the BeamLayout / RayModel laws unchanged (AGENTS.md 'One ray law').\n- Placing an element binds a slot. The constructor model keeps the active setup and writes it through KitProxy.\n\nMessages CreateSetup, AssignSlot and SwapSlot are pure updates with tests. S8.1's run law reads the setup's slots in light order.\n\nGates: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests, ui-smoke, and ui-tests by touched class.", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Scene.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/BeamLayout.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Placement.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentRun.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs"], "invariants": ["ASSERT_INVARIANT s26-elev-list-empty must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"ELEV0\" -- Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s26-no-vstest must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk|xunit.runner.visualstudio|Xunit.SkippableFact|IsTestingPlatformApplication\" -- \"*.fsproj\" \"*.props\" \"*.targets\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s26-no-kit-kit-json must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"kit.kit-json\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s26-no-eps-axis-evaluated must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"EpsAxisEvaluated\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s26-complexity-mandatory must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"complexity = (None|Some)\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s26-no-seeded-string-preset-ids must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"(src-(600|hene-|ar-4|ar-5|hecd-|diode-|ruby-|tisa-|ndyag-|er-1550|co2-|hg-|krf-|arf-|f2-1|euv-|beuv-|xe-mono|supercontinuum)|det-(intensity|ellipsometer)|pol-(lp|cp-left|cp-right))\" -- \"Berreman/*.fs\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s26-no-seeding-seam must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"SeedingProxy|seedAll|OpticalConstructor.Seeding\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s26-t1-no-code-seeds must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"let (builtInEntries|seedEntries|standardCategories) \" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s26-no-seed-modules must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"SeedSamples|SeedSources|SeedEntryIds\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s26-no-test-db must-find-nothing: git grep -n -w -E \"TestDbContext|DatabaseProvider|databaseProvider|OpticalConstructorMssql\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s26-no-versions-in-use must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"VersionsInUse|versionsInUseSeam\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s26-no-scene-collection-seams must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"SceneProxy|ExperimentCollectionProxy\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s26-t4-no-ocproj must-find-nothing: git grep -n -i -F \"ocproj\" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s26-no-recent-json must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"recent.json\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s26-no-measured-element-of must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"measuredElementOf\" -- Berreman/"]}
{"number": 27, "name": "S8.3 -- The naming template and the grid generator", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor 001 sec J ('Naming template', 'Grid generator'), sec R ('MuellerExperimentLabel.parsed and experimentRegex') and sec P GenerateSetupGrid. Soft budget: 10-18 steps.\n\nDomain NamingTemplate, one per kit, carried in .kit-json (e.g. '{source}-({obj1}#{phi1}-{obj2}#{phi2})-{analyzer}-{note}'):\n- It FORMATS a setup or experiment name from its slots and angles, and PARSES a name back into slot items and angles, to match imported data.\n- It replaces MuellerExperimentLabel.parsed and its experimentRegex / objectRegex (MuellerReconstruction.fs).\n  - Their cases become the template engine's first tests: MuellerReconstructionTests' label facts (e.g. 'CPL-(QZ#90-LR#90)-CPL', the AIR rows, the note suffix, non-matching labels).\n  - Every caller of parsed (the ParsedExperiment family / objectRotation / matrixKind users in Domain and BerremanTests) reads the template's parse instead.\n  - The regexes and parsed are deleted.\n- Names keep the lab's characters; .spec-md sec 3.11 applies to file names only.\n\nGrid generator (Domain, pure):\n- A set of options per slot gives their product; impossible or unwanted combinations are unticked; every setup and experiment is then created at once (GenerateSetupGrid), named by the template.\n\nTests: the moved label cases; format then parse is the identity; the grid product with exclusions.\n\nThis establishes 001 sec T 'From section 8'.\n\nGates: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests, unit-tests (MuellerReconstructionTests; its label facts move or are re-pointed), and ui-tests by touched class.", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs"], "invariants": ["ASSERT_INVARIANT s27-elev-list-empty must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"ELEV0\" -- Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s27-no-vstest must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk|xunit.runner.visualstudio|Xunit.SkippableFact|IsTestingPlatformApplication\" -- \"*.fsproj\" \"*.props\" \"*.targets\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s27-no-kit-kit-json must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"kit.kit-json\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s27-no-eps-axis-evaluated must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"EpsAxisEvaluated\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s27-complexity-mandatory must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"complexity = (None|Some)\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s27-no-seeded-string-preset-ids must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"(src-(600|hene-|ar-4|ar-5|hecd-|diode-|ruby-|tisa-|ndyag-|er-1550|co2-|hg-|krf-|arf-|f2-1|euv-|beuv-|xe-mono|supercontinuum)|det-(intensity|ellipsometer)|pol-(lp|cp-left|cp-right))\" -- \"Berreman/*.fs\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s27-no-seeding-seam must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"SeedingProxy|seedAll|OpticalConstructor.Seeding\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s27-t1-no-code-seeds must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"let (builtInEntries|seedEntries|standardCategories) \" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s27-no-seed-modules must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"SeedSamples|SeedSources|Seed