{"number": 29, "name": "S9.1 -- Experiments v2: scans, roles, sessions and attachments", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor 001 sec K ('Experiment = one recorded run...', 'Status badges'), sec E ('notes on experiments ... live in their files') and sec P SetExperimentRole. Soft budget: 12-20 steps.\n\nExperiments.fs Experiment v2:\n- A setup reference (S8.2).\n- A scan of one or more variables: dial 0..360 in steps of 20; phi; incidence x azimuth x observable; lambda on a tunable source, within its limits. Today's VariableParameter / VariableRange / sourceWaveLengthOpt are generalised, not duplicated.\n- A capture (T / R, from the detectors).\n- A role: ScienceRun | CalibrationRun | DarkRun | DriftCheckRun | DiagnosticRun | IgnoredRun | PlannedRun, with int wire tags.\n- A session and notes.\n- The data attachment: a DataAttachment + an import-profile name + a row selection (profiles arrive in S9.2).\n- Experiments are named by the kit's naming template (S8.3) and stored as <name>.experiment-json.\n\nStatus badges (pure): no data / mapped / validated (points) / excluded points / data changed (S4.2's hash) / out of range.\n\nThe Experiments bay, the experiment chart (ExperimentChart.fs, chartForRun) and the export path read v2. Today's single-variable experiments are one-variable scans.\n\nGates: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests, ui-smoke, and ui-tests by touched class (FsxAcceptanceTests, ExperimentControlsTests, Workbenc