{"number": 30, "name": "S9.2 -- Import profiles and the column-mapping wizard", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor 001 sec K ('Column-mapping import wizard' and its built-in profiles), sec R ('The strict v1 X,Y path') and sec P AttachDataFile. Soft budget: 12-22 steps.\n\nDomain ImportProfile (named, stored in .kit-json):\n- the delimiter, the header row and the BOM;\n- column roles: scan variable(s) with unit and raw-dial vs physical, signal, sigma, timestamp, capture index, experiment key; or Mueller elements m00..m33 plus configuration columns.\n\nBuilt-in profiles REUSE the parsers:\n- MeasuredData DataFileText.parseIntensitySeries / parseEllipsometricSeries (intensity, Psi / Delta);\n- MuellerDataStore DataFileText.parseMuellerCsv, as the 'Phone ROI CSV' profile;\n- a NEW Mueller-matrix observation profile: normalized m00..m33 + absolute throughput + the configuration columns (incidence, azimuth, observable, cut / sample), in the 0044 MuellerInverse.MuellerObservation shape. It also WRITES files; AT-2 writes its observations through it.\n\nThe strict v1 path is deleted: the fixed-schema attach in ExperimentDataProxy, ExperimentDataStore.createFileBacked and ExperimentDataLoad is replaced by attach-with-profile. AttachDataFile takes the file, copies it in or records it in place (S4.2), applies a profile, and gives mapped points. The parsers survive only as profiles.\n\nThe wizard (its own view and window):\n- sniff the delimiter, header and BOM; preview; map columns to roles; pick or save a named profile.\n- Ids, keepOnScreen, ScrollExtentTests.\n\nTests: each built-in profile reads its fixture exactly as its parser did; the observation profile round-trips; a custom mapping; sniffing.\n\nGates: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests, ui-smoke, and ui-tests by touched class (DataFilePickerFolderTests, InverseConstructorTests, ...).", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MeasuredData.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataProxy.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/ExperimentDataStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/MuellerDataStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MeasuredDataTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataStoreTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataFilePickerFolderTests.fs"], "invariants": ["ASSERT_INVARIANT s30-elev-list-empty must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"ELEV0\" -- Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s30-no-vstest must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk|xunit.runner.visualstudio|Xunit.SkippableFact|IsTestingPlatformApplication\" -- \"*.fsproj\" \"*.props\" \"*.targets\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s30-no-kit-kit-json must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"kit.kit-json\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s30-no-eps-axis-evaluated must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"EpsAxisEvaluated\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s30-complexity-mandatory must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"complexity = (None|Some)\" --