{"number": 36, "name": "S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor 001 sec L ('Study grows from the experiment collection...', 'Scope is the sharing rule', 'Sessions and gain models as data'), sec I ('Material parameters as unknowns'), sec N ('Parameter-axis generation'), sec E's notes, and sec P (CreateStudy, AddExperimentsToStudy, OpenMaterial, SetParameterScope, LinkParameters), with .spec-md sec 3.16. Soft budget: 14-24 steps.\n\nDomain Study (<name>.study-json), a named set of experiments of ONE kit:\n- The unknowns, each with an owner (item / material / session / experiment) and a scope: ItemScope | MaterialScope | SessionScope | ExperimentScope.\n- Links as constraints ('CPL2.delta = CPL1.delta').\n- Sessions, auto-split at DiagnosticRun experiments or set by hand. Per session a gain model (free; anchored to its AIR runs; interpolated between two AIR repeats), and dark from the DarkRun experiments. MuellerReconstruction.familyGain (with its GainCalibration cases) becomes these models' first implementation, moved, not copied.\n- Fit settings (joint / staged, S11.3), weights per experiment or per detector, enable / disable per experiment, and notes.\n\nMaterial physics form:\n- A material version may hold one of the three crystal-parameter records (UniaxialParameters, TriclinicParameters, AbsorbingTriclinicParameters) as its physics: a new case beside the existing complexity tree, with toProperties through the S10.1 builders.\n- The editor, the facets and the entry-file schema follow.\n\nOpenMaterial:\n- A study opens a material version into a study-local working copy, stored in the study file. Every component is a Parameter, UnknownParameter where the user frees it.\n- Every sample made of it shares them (MaterialScope).\n\nGenerated axes:\n- A material's or item model's published ParameterAxis list.\n- The EXACT test: the generated axes of an opened AbsorbingTriclinicParameters material equal AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.axes (names, order, field kinds, read / write on a probe).\n\nThe messages are pure updates, with tests over in-memory kits.\n\nGates: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests, and unit-tests (MuellerReconstructionTests, because familyGain moves; plus a cheap MuellerInverse class if MuellerInverse.fs is touched).", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs"], "invariants": ["ASSERT_INVARIANT s36-elev-list-empty must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"ELEV0\" -- Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s36-no-vstest must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk|xunit.runner.visualstudio|Xunit.SkippableFact|IsTestingPlatformApplication\" -- \"*.fsproj\" \"*.props\" \"*.targets\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s36-no-kit-kit-json must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"kit.kit-json\" -- Berreman/"