{"number": 38, "name": "S11.3 -- Engines, staged and joint fits, and append-only fit runs", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor 001 sec L ('Fit modes', 'Engines -- the existing ones, reused'), sec E ('Fit runs are append-only and store the full parameter vector'), sec N ('Long fits run on JobRunner') and sec P (RunFit, and PublishCalibration as the stage hand-off). Soft budget: 12-22 steps.\n\nThe study engine (Optimization, a new file) chooses its engine automatically:\n- LINEAR when the unknowns enter linearly, e.g. black-box Mueller objects with calibrated instruments: S10.3's staged path / MuellerReconstruction.buildDesign + reconstruct through MuellerSolverProxy.\n- NONLINEAR otherwise: MuellerInverseSolver.createAlglibLevenbergMarquardt over MuellerInverse.forwardModels and the S10.1 fit wrappers, multi-start, driven by the generated axes. The start is the parameters' start values, the bounds come from their states, and priors are residual rows with sigma.\n\nModes:\n- Joint: every unknown at once.\n- Staged: stage 1 calibrates items on CalibrationRun experiments (the Eigenvalue Calibration Method path over the AIR runs); 'Publish calibration' (S11.5's revision write) then feeds stage 2, which fits the objects with those values fixed, or as priors with sigma.\n\nFitRun (<study>@<stamp>.fitrun-json):\n- The stamp comes from ClockProvider. Fit runs are append-only and never rewritten.\n- A run holds the full parameter vector used and produced, the mode and stage, the data hashes it read, and notes. S11.4 fills in the results.\n\nLong fits run on JobRunner (OpticalConstructor.Ui/JobRunner.fs) with per-iteration progress and Cancel. The fit run is written on completion only.\n\nTests: the engine choice; small synthetic linear and nonlinear studies recover their truth; the staged hand-off fixes the stage-1 values; fit runs never overwrite.\n\nGates: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests, unit-tests by class if Optimization's shared code is touched (name cheap classes), and ui-tests (JobRunner hosting).", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerInverseSolver.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/InverseFit.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FitQuality.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/JobRunner.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/JobRunnerCancelTests.fs"], "invariants": ["ASSERT_INVARIANT s38-elev-list-empty must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"ELEV0\" -- Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s38-no-vstest must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk|xunit.runner.visualstudio|Xunit.SkippableFact|IsTestingPlatformApplication\" -- \"*.fsproj\" \"*.props\" \"*.targets\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s38-no-kit-kit-json must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"kit.kit-json\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s38-no-eps-axis-evaluated must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"EpsAxisEvaluated\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s38-complexity-mandatory must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"complexity = (None|Some)\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s38-no-seeded-string-preset-ids 