{"number": 39, "name": "S11.4 -- Fit results: uncertainty, correlation, realizability, product check, profile likelihood", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor 001 sec L 'Results, stored in the fit run'. Soft budget: 8-14 steps.\n\nThe fit run records:\n- value +/- sigma from the Jacobian covariance (REUSE FitQuality.FitReport / standardErrors);\n- the correlation matrix, the rank and the condition, through the MuellerInverse.ResidualJacobian carrier (correlation, conditionNumber, columnNorms);\n- per-experiment residuals and RMSE;\n- Mueller realizability for every black-box object: coherency eigenvalues >= 0 (REUSE MuellerInverse.CoherencyEigenvalue and the coherency members beside it);\n- the product check for objects in series: M_comb against M_LR . M_QZ (REUSE MuellerReconstruction.cascadeProduct and the RMSE ratio S10.3 computes);\n- post-fit identifiability by profile likelihood, for parameters flagged suspect (correlation or sigma above thresholds stated in the fit settings): re-fit with the parameter stepped across its sigma range, and record the chi-squared profile.\n\nTests on synthetic studies: an identifiable pair against a confounded pair.\n\nGates: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests.", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FitQuality.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/O