{"number": 41, "name": "S12.1 -- AT-1 and the optics-mueller reference kit", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor 001 sec 1a, sec Q ('Common rules' and 'AT-1') and sec U kit-acceptance, with .spec-md secs 3.12, 3.13 and 3.21. Soft budget: 10-18 steps.\n\nCreate Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitAcceptanceTests.fs: trait Category=kit-acceptance, in the FsxAcceptanceTests pattern (the headless app, semantic messages only). From this step on, the kit-acceptance gate runs on every step that touches the study, the run law, the import code, the acceptance file or the kits.\n\nBuild:\n- Copy the committed data/optics-mueller/data/ tree into a fresh folder under the test output.\n- Against a SQLite :memory: library filled from Catalogue/Builtin, through messages only:\n  - New kit on that folder: name, author, and the lab naming template '{source}-({obj1}#{phi1}-{obj2}#{phi2})-{analyzer}-{note}';\n  - the items: the laser, LP1, LP2, CPL1 / CPL2 (compound LP + retarder, with delta and the axis offset unknown), QZ / LR (black-box Mueller), and the phone (an intensity detector with session gain and dark);\n  - the setups, by the grid over 4 families x {AIR, QZ, LR, QZ then LR} x phi. The two-sample setups put QZ in Object 1 and LR in Object 2;\n  - attach data/raw/final/*.csv in place through the Phone ROI CSV profile; split by 'experiment'; match by the template;\n  - the roles: DarkRun for Darkness, DiagnosticRun for BullshitCheck, and the AIR repeats -BR / -2R;\n  - the LR correction (the setup re-pointed to -45 / -90, with an audit note) and the excluded frame, as data;\n  - the staged study: stage 1 AIR calibration, publish, stage 2 objects.\n- Everything is written through the REAL folder KitProxy.\n\nCreate the committed kit ONCE: run the build and copy its output into data/optics-mueller/, around the lab files S9.4 moved there (.oc/ excluded), and commit it. It is never hand-written.\n\nAssertions:\n- The built kit equals the committed kit, file by file: every kit file, library/** and data/**, with .oc/ excluded.\n- Open the COMMITTED kit read-only (nothing written, .spec-md sec 3.12) against an EMPTY library database, and run its study.\n- M_QZ, M_LR, M_{QZ+LR}, the CPL retardances, the angle offset and the dial zeros are within dataMatrixTol of S10.3's shared reference module; so is the product-check RMSE ratio.\n- Send round trip: SendKit zips the kit, it is unzipped under the test output and reopened; the reopened kit, and the study's residual vector at its start point, equal the built ones.\n\nGates: build, elevation, kit-acceptance (the AT-1 class), ui-tests by touched class, and unit-tests (MuellerReconstructionTests) if the reference module is touched.", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj", ".gates/OpticalConstructor/kit-acceptance.gates", "data/optics-mueller/", "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs"], "invariants": ["ASSERT_INVARIANT s41-elev-list-empty must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"ELEV0\" -- Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s41-no-vstest must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk|xunit.runner.visualstudio|Xu