{"number": 42, "name": "S12.2 -- AT-2 and the absorbing-biaxial-noisy reference kit", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor 001 sec 1b and sec Q ('Common rules' and 'AT-2'). Soft budget: 10-18 steps.\n\nBuild, through messages, against SQLite :memory::\n- a source at referenceWaveLength;\n- an ideal Mueller-polarimeter detector with the NoiseParam.decentLab noise model;\n- ONE material version holding the 'absorbing' ground truth (AbsorbingTriclinicParameters physics, S11.1);\n- five sample items, all of that material: 100 um plates cut opticAxisCut, otherOpticAxisCut, Z, X and Y (BerremanTestSupport AbsorbingBiaxialSample);\n- one experiment per plate, whose multi-variable scan (incidence x azimuth x T / R) reproduces exactly a1 @ a2 @ a3 = fullConfigurations. The grid generator produces them, checked configuration by configuration.\n\nData:\n- For each of the five seeds, the observations come from the EXISTING 'noisyObserveAbsoluteWith forward absorbing NoiseParam.decentLab seed fullConfigurations' (S10.1's product function).\n- They are written as kit data files under the kit's data/ through S9.2's Mueller-matrix observation profile, and read back through the same profile.\n\nStudy: open the material with all 15 components UnknownParameter (MaterialScope across the five plates); start = perturbedStart, box = searchBox.\n\nCreate the committed data/absorbing-biaxial-noisy/ by running the build once (with its five observation files), and commit it. The test regenerates the files from the seeds and requires them byte-identical to the committed ones.\n\nAssertions, cheap to expensive:\n1. Data identity: the observations the study loads equal the harness's exactly.\n2. Model identity: the generated axes equal AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.axes, and the study's residual vector at perturbedStart equals throughputResidualFor's (<= 1e-12 relative).\n3. Fit: one seed through the study engine recovers the 15 constants and the derived quantities (birefringences, isotropic absorption) within the bands AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests asserts. MOVE those band checks into one shared function in BerremanTestSupport that both tests call.\n4. The full five-seed ensemble, through the reused statisticsFor: marked xUnit v3 Explicit (about 16 minutes; run on demand).\nAlso: the built kit equals the committed one file by file; a read-only open of the committed kit against an empty library runs 1-3; and the Send round trip runs as in AT-1.\n\nGates: build, elevation, kit-acceptance (the AT-2 class), unit-tests (AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests, whose bands moved), and ui-tests by touched class.", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj", "data/absorbing-biaxial-noisy/"], "invariants": ["ASSERT_INVARIANT s42-elev-list-empty must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"ELEV0\" -- Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s42-no-vstest must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk|xunit.runner.visualstudio|Xunit.SkippableFact|IsTestingPlatformApplication\" -- \"*.fsproj\" \"*.props\" \"*.targets\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s42-no-kit-kit-json must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"kit.kit-json\" 