{"number": 43, "name": "S13.1 -- MaterialSourceProxy and refractiveindex.info", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor 001 sec D (item 1; 'A pulled record becomes a user material version...'; 'Updating a source mints a NEW version') and sec P MaterialSourceProxy. Soft budget: 12-20 steps.\n\nMaterialSourceProxy (a record and an in-memory double in Domain; a Storage create):\n- search, fetch and update the snapshot, per adapter;\n- HTTP goes through one seam ([<ElevationBoundary>]), and no test calls it; tests use fixture snapshots under the test output.\n\nThe refractiveindex.info adapter (CC0):\n- An offline snapshot of the GitHub database (polyanskiy/refractiveindex.info-database) lives under a DataLocations sources folder.\n- 'Update snapshot' downloads the current archive, with per-file progress and Cancel (.spec-md sec 10).\n- Search runs over the snapshot's catalog. A record is parsed by REUSING MaterialImport (RefractiveIndexInfoText: tabulated and formula pages, with S1.1's tabulated case).\n\nPulled records:\n- A pulled record becomes a USER material version in the database, with pulled-from-source provenance (source, record path, snapshot date or commit, licence CC0, citation) and a pulled-source record row (S2.1).\n- Updating the snapshot re-fetches the pulled records and mints a NEW version only where a record's hash changed. Nothing mutates.\n\nMaterials window: an 'Online sources...' search and fetch UI (ids, keepOnScreen, ScrollExtentTests).\n\nTests over a fixture snapshot: search; a pull gives version 1 with provenance; an unchanged update makes no new version; a changed record gives version 2.\n\nGates: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests, ui-smoke, and ui-tests by touched class.", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialImportTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/fixtures/", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/WorkbenchSettings.fs"], "invariants": ["ASSERT_INVARIANT s43-elev-list-empty must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"ELEV0\" -- Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s43-no-vstest must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk|xunit.runner.visualstudio|Xunit.SkippableFact|IsTestingPlatformApplication\" -- \"*.fsproj\" \"*.props\" \"*.targets\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s43-no-kit-kit-json must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"kit.kit-json\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s43-no-eps-axis-evaluated must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"EpsAxisEvaluated\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s43-complexity-mandatory must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"complexity = (None|Some)\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s43-no-seeded-string-preset-ids must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"(src-(600|hene-|ar-4|ar-5|hecd-|diode-|ruby-|tisa-|ndyag-|er-1550|co2-|hg-|krf-|arf-|f2-1|euv-|beuv-|xe-mono|supercontinuum)|det-(intensity|ellipsometer)|pol-(lp|cp-left|cp-right))\" -- \"Berreman/*.fs\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s43-no-seeding-seam must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"SeedingProxy|seedAll|OpticalConstructor.Seeding\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s43-t1-no-code-seeds must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"let (builtInEntries|seedEn