{"number": 44, "name": "S13.2 -- PTB OCDB, the Henke compound calculator and glass catalogues", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor 001 sec D (items 2-3; 'Uncertainties travel with the material ... become priors in studies and inputs to the Planner'; 'User-supplied glass catalogues ... import only, never bundle'), with .spec-md sec 3.19. Soft budget: 12-20 steps.\n\nThe PTB OCDB adapter (CC BY 4.0):\n- EUV / VUV n, k WITH uncertainties. S1.1's tabulated case gains optional per-sample sigma-n / sigma-k arrays (data, serialised).\n- A study that opens such a material (S11.1) takes sigma as its components' prior, and the Planner (S14) reads them as prior inputs.\n- The attribution shows (S3.3, CC-BY).\n\nThe Henke compound calculator:\n- CXRO atomic scattering factors f1, f2 per element are fetched once through the proxy and kept in the snapshot folder.\n- With a chemical formula and a density they give n, k over the EUV / X-ray range, as a tabulated user material with provenance (CXRO, citation).\n\nAGF import (Schott / Ohara / Hoya / CDGM):\n- A user-supplied .agf file becomes user materials. Their formula coefficients are lowered through MaterialImport's existing formula lowering, with imported-from-file provenance. Nothing is bundled.\n\nThere is no adapter for Materials Project, paywalled sources, or gyration / magneto-optic data (.spec-md sec 8).\n\nTests over fixtures: a PTB record with sigma; two element .nff files and a formula; a small AGF file.\n\nGates: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests, and ui-tests by touched class.", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/fixtures/"], "invariants": ["ASSERT_INVARIANT s44-elev-list-empty must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"ELEV0\" -- Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s44-no-vstest must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk|xunit.runner.visualstudio|Xunit.SkippableFact|IsTestingPlatformApplication\" -- \"*.fsproj\" \"*.props\" \"*.targets\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s44-no-kit-kit-json must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"kit.kit-json\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s44-no-eps-axis-evaluated must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"EpsAxisEvaluated\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s44-complexity-mandatory must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"complexity = (None|Some)\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s44-no-seeded-string-preset-ids must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"(src-(600|hene-|ar-4|ar-5|hecd-|diode-|ruby-|tisa-|ndyag-|er-1550|co2-|hg-|krf-|arf-|f2-1|euv-|beuv-|xe-mono|supercontinuum)|det-(intensity|ellipsometer)|pol-(lp|cp-left|cp-right))\" -- \"Berreman/*.fs\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s44-no-seeding-seam must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"SeedingProxy|seedAll|OpticalConstructor.Seeding\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s44-t1-no-code-seeds must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"let (builtInEntries|seedEntries|standardCategories) \" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s44-no-seed-modules must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"SeedSamples|SeedSources|SeedEntryIds\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s44-no-test-db must-find-nothing: git grep -n -w -E \"TestDbContext|DatabaseProvid