{"number": 45, "name": "S14.1 -- The Measurement Planner: kit inputs and the structural layer", "brief": "Read specs/0050/.spec-md first. Its sections 0-10 bind every section: the wiring contract, precedence, the interpretations of sec 3, the constraints of sec 4, the shared shapes of sec 5, reuse, migration intent, negative scope, verification and gates, and the UX commitments. 001 (specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md) is the requirement; read the parts this brief names. Choose each step's gates by .user-md/spec-author.user-md 'Choosing a step's gates'. kit-acceptance is not runnable before S12.1 creates KitAcceptanceTests.fs.\n\nAuthor 001 sec M ('Target', 'Its inputs are the kit', 'Layer 1, structural' and its acceptance facts) with specs/0044/.manual/004-active-anisotropic-inverse-problem.md (the physics) and 017-feasible-biaxial-experiments.md (the binormal plate). Soft budget: 10-18 steps.\n\nInputs (Domain, pure, from the kit only):\n- lab profile: the kit's items, i.e. sources and lambda ranges, polarizers, compensators, compounds, detectors, angle ranges, and each detector's noise model (S7.1's Domain noise types);\n- sample inventory: the sample items (cuts, thicknesses, substrates);\n- prior: KnownParameter / CalibratedParameter values, the material class or point group, the dispersion choices, and source uncertainties (PTB sigma, S13.2);\n- targets: the study's chosen unknowns.\n\nLayer 1 (exact, tabulated, Domain):\n- the point group fixes the independent tensor components: isotropic 1, uniaxial 2, biaxial 3 + orientation;\n- optical activity in 18 of the 21 non-centrosymmetric classes;\n- what each cut sees: a c-cut at normal incidence sees n_o only (and g33); n_e needs oblique incidence or an a-cut; Snell caps the internal angle (REUSE MuellerInverse.internalAngle, gyrationProjection and orientForCut);\n- activity along birefringent directions needs full-Mueller or HAUP-class detection;\n- low symmetry needs several cuts x azimuths x angles;\n- intensity-only detectors lose phase.\nIt outputs 'this kit can never recover X' and 'you need an off-axis cut' findings.\n\nAcceptance REUSES the existing facts' designs and helpers; no new physics test is written:\n- For MuellerInverseTests' C1-only design, the report says C1 is blind to g33 and leaves three of the four constants unrecoverable, and proposes the second cut.\n- For a normal-incidence-only BiaxialInverseTests design, it flags g12, g13 and g23 as unrecoverable, and names oblique incidence and further cuts as the remedy.\nThe facts live in BerremanTests (a new planner class) beside the designs they reuse. Move a design definition into BerremanTestSupport if a fact needs it outside its class.\n\nGates: build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests, and unit-tests (the new planner class, plus any class whose design moved).", "pointers": ["specs/0050/.spec-md", "specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/", "specs/0044/.manual/004-active-anisotropic-inverse-problem.md", "specs/0044/.manual/017-feasible-biaxial-experiments.md", "specs/0046/.manual/018-sharing-libraries-inverse-planner.md"], "invariants": ["ASSERT_INVARIANT s45-elev-list-empty must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"ELEV0\" -- Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s45-no-vstest must-find-nothing: git grep -n -E \"Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk|xunit.runner.visualstudio|Xunit.SkippableFact|IsTestingPlatformApplication\" -- \"*.fsproj\" \"*.props\" \"*.targets\"", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s45-no-kit-kit-json must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"kit.kit-json\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s45-no-eps-axis-evaluated must-find-nothing: git grep -n -F \"EpsAxisEvaluated\" -- Berreman/", "ASSERT_INVARIANT s45-complexity-mandatory mu